{"caseId":"OD2-DEV2-SEQ","methodChoice":"Compared where the days are lost, step by step and by loan type, against the dates of each change. Then read the policy wording and the withdrawal reasons.","answers":[{"itemId":"Q-H1","answer":"contradicted","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["X15","E2","E3","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q-H2","answer":"contradicted","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["E2","X15","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q-H3","answer":"supported","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X3","X15","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q-H4","answer":"contradicted","confidence":72,"evidenceIds":["X15","E5","X3"]},{"itemId":"Q-H5","answer":"unknown","confidence":50,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q-H6","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X15","E2","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q-R1","answer":"causal","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X3","X15","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q-R2","answer":"association-only","confidence":50,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q-R3","answer":"contradicted","confidence":78,"evidenceIds":["X15","E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q-R4","answer":"contradicted","confidence":72,"evidenceIds":["X15","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q-A1","answer":"preferred","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X3","X15"]},{"itemId":"Q-A2","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X15","E3","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q-A3","answer":"premature","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["X4","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q-A4","answer":"harmful","confidence":65,"evidenceIds":["X15","E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q-A5","answer":"acceptable","confidence":50,"evidenceIds":["X15","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q-SUFF","answer":"sufficient","confidence":72,"evidenceIds":["X15","X3"]}],"brief":"Nearly all the slowdown is in one step: collateral valuation on property-secured loans. It took 1.6 days in March and 1.7 in April, then 7.6 in June and 8.4 in August. Other steps barely moved; unsecured loans are back to normal. The jump follows the 1 May credit policy refresh, which lowered the loan size needing a full inspection appraisal from $500k to $150k; nobody assessed the processing-time effect. The valuation firm's April renewal brought no slowdown, Corvane caused only a short April bump, new-hire branches match the others, and Credit Hub underwriting is flat. I'm about 85–90% sure; I haven't seen the valuation firm's own turnaround figures.

Withdrawals are less clear: 32 of 73 recent closures are new automatic closures of files inactive for 30 days, which the old system never counted, so the rise may be mostly a counting change.

Next: don't withhold Corvane's payment or put new hires on improvement plans. Take the measured delay and the audit rationale (desktop valuations overstated by a median 12%) to the credit risk committee to decide on the threshold. Add a by-stage view to the dashboard, report automatic closures separately, and hold off on fee rebates."}
